{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQASu9wVEJ9TVWnhHwtE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't remove anything, because `legacy_orders` is still in use.\n\n`scripts/monthly-report.js:5` reads from it. The file says finance runs this report on the 1st of each month, and it pulls pre-2024 revenue from `legacy_orders` for the year-over-year comparison. If the table were dropped, the next monthly report would fail. Since `scripts/migrate.js` runs migrations against the production database, removing the table would also delete the imported historical orders, and that can't be undone.\n\nThat one script is the only thing that uses it. Nothing in `src/`, the tests or the other migrations touches it.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n\n1. **The report doesn't need the historical numbers anymore** (for example, the 3-year lookback now lands in 2024 or later, where `orders` has the data). I can take the `historical` query out of the report and add a `003_drop_legacy_orders.sql` migration. Finance should confirm first, and you'd want a backup or export of the table before running it.\n2. **The report still needs the data.** I can move the legacy rows into `orders`, converting `amount` to `total_cents` and `placed_on` to `created_at`, point the report at `orders`, and then drop the table.\n3. **Leave it as is** if it's only clutter.\n\nWhich one do you want?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":739,"cache_read_input_tokens":30731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":739},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2bc64d1-c10c-4d7a-ab23-7e94812cccfc","uuid":"dc5c8927-51ff-4fdf-9daa-77700dcb0abb","timestamp":"2026